From 84be0119d0cf82e0e9a3bcebeda0c133539a86ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 20:41:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] bluestore: split read into
 bluestore_read/get_onode/_do_read sub-spans + accept parent trace

Once librados gained an IoCtx::operate read overload accepting
jspan_context, RGW GETs propagate OTel context to the OSD and
op->osd_parent_span becomes a real recording span on the read path.
This commit threads that context down through the read pipeline so
BlueStore-level spans link under the OSD's read trace instead of
being orphan roots.

  * ObjectStore::read virtual gains an optional jspan_context*
    parent_trace param (default nullptr; existing callers unchanged).
  * BlueStore::read and MemStore::read overrides updated.
  * BlueStore::read replaces the orphan start_trace with a
    parent-aware add_span and adds two child spans inside the
    function: get_onode (kv lookup latency) and _do_read (the
    actual BlueFS/bdev extent read).
  * PGBackend::objects_read_sync and ReplicatedBackend's override
    take a parent context; ReplicatedBackend passes it to store->read.
  * PrimaryLogPG.cc updated at the four objects_read_sync call
    sites (main CEPH_OSD_OP_READ, the hit-set-archive direct read,
    the chunk-read path, the dedup base read) to pass
    ctx->op->osd_parent_span's context.

After this, a GET trace fans out:
  rgw_request -> rados_read -> op-request-created -> dequeue_op
   -> do_op -> execute_ctx -> bluestore_read -> {get_onode, _do_read}

bluestore::tracer spans surface as service.name=bluestore in Tempo,
and Prometheus span-metrics gain traces_spanmetrics_latency_bucket
{service=bluestore, span_name=bluestore_read|get_onode|_do_read}
per OSD.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
